# Per-category app time budgets: allow the parental-controls app to freeze/thaw
# ONLY its own cgroups (parental-<username>-<category>) and to move PIDs into
# them. No signals, no SIGKILL anywhere in budget enforcement.
# Install as /etc/sudoers.d/parental-controls-budgets (mode 0440) and check
# with `visudo -c`.
#
# Both /usr/sbin and /usr/bin are listed: the code invokes bare names
# (`sudo tee`, `sudo cat`, `sudo mkdir`) and sudo resolves them via
# secure_path (sbin first). sudo matches on the path string.
#
# ARGUMENTS ARE REGEX-ANCHORED. sudoers(5): "If the arguments in a Cmnd begin
# with the '^' character, they will be interpreted as a regular expression and
# matched accordingly" -- the regex covers the ARGUMENTS ONLY, after the
# command path. A trailing-wildcard argument form is unsafe because sudo
# matches arguments as one concatenated string and `*` spans '/', so
# `parental-*/cgroup.procs` also matched
# `parental-x/../system.slice/sshd.service/cgroup.procs` (an arbitrary PID
# migration/freeze primitive). The patterns below pin each argument exactly.
# `[.]` keeps dots literal; the username/category segment cannot contain '/'.
# See sudo-audit.md §2 and §5 Step 3.
#
# PAM SESSIONS DISABLED FOR THE SERVICE USER'S SUDO CHILDREN — the same
# Defaults entry documented in depth in the sudoers-parental-controls
# template. Short version: every sudo opens a PAM session that pam_systemd
# registers with logind; logind caps a user at MaxSessions (default 5)
# class-user sessions, and the budget-tick sudo bursts (tee/cat/mkdir on
# every pass, plus the status probes) blew through it:
# TooManySessions -> `pam_open_session: Permission denied` -> sudo died
# before running the command. `Defaults:` scopes to the INVOKING user list
# (sudoers(5); `Defaults!` is command scope — do not switch it), and
# `!pam_session` (sudo >= 1.8.7) skips the session phase. Lost: only
# sudo's session open/close journal lines and PAM resource limits for this
# user's non-interactive sudo; auth/account phases and sudo's command
# logging still run. Repeated here because sudoers merges both files and
# each must stay effective on its own. Supersedes the
# XDG_SESSION_CLASS=background unit workaround, which remains as
# belt-and-braces; see AGENT_CONTEXT.md "Status right now".
Defaults:@SERVICE_USER@ !pam_session
@SERVICE_USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/tee ^/sys/fs/cgroup/parental-[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/cgroup[.]freeze$, /usr/bin/tee ^/sys/fs/cgroup/parental-[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/cgroup[.]freeze$
@SERVICE_USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/tee ^/sys/fs/cgroup/parental-[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/cgroup[.]procs$, /usr/bin/tee ^/sys/fs/cgroup/parental-[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/cgroup[.]procs$
@SERVICE_USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/cat ^/sys/fs/cgroup/parental-[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/cgroup[.]freeze$, /usr/bin/cat ^/sys/fs/cgroup/parental-[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/cgroup[.]freeze$
@SERVICE_USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/cat ^/sys/fs/cgroup/parental-[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/cgroup[.]procs$, /usr/bin/cat ^/sys/fs/cgroup/parental-[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/cgroup[.]procs$
@SERVICE_USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/mkdir ^-p /sys/fs/cgroup/parental-[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$, /usr/bin/mkdir ^-p /sys/fs/cgroup/parental-[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$
